  "course": {
    "narrative": "A 45-year-old female presented with severe (9/10) left lower jaw pain starting overnight, associated with a fractured tooth and likely dental abscess. Her past medical history includes CAD, hypertension, and hypothyroidism. Physical examination revealed significant dental decay and a small fracture on tooth #20 with a minor area of fluctuance and induration. In the ED, she received an inferior alveolar nerve block with 1.5 mL of 0.5% bupivacaine, which provided mild pain relief. She was also administered two Vicodin and a dose of Keflex, which she tolerated well without hypersensitivity. She was prescribed Vicodin and Keflex, instructed to follow up with the Dental Clinic on Monday, and discharged in satisfactory condition.",
